From: cubie-a5e-openwrt <noreply@github.com>
Subject: sunxi: cortexa55: enable the PCI/PCIe features

The A527 has a PCIe root complex (the Cubie A5E M.2 slot) and PR #23296
builds its driver (CONFIG_PCIE_SUN55I_RC=y), but the subtarget does not
declare the pci/pcie features, so packages that depend on PCI_SUPPORT
(kmod-nvme, pciutils) cannot be selected.

---
diff --git a/target/linux/sunxi/cortexa55/target.mk b/target/linux/sunxi/cortexa55/target.mk
index 5941f31f..7ea23e68 100644
--- a/target/linux/sunxi/cortexa55/target.mk
+++ b/target/linux/sunxi/cortexa55/target.mk
@@ -8,4 +8,4 @@ ARCH:=aarch64
 BOARDNAME:=Allwinner A52x/T52x (cortexa55)
 CPU_TYPE:=cortex-a55
 KERNELNAME:=Image dtbs
-FEATURES+=fpu
+FEATURES+=fpu pci pcie
